description:
FOUND AND FIXED by s535a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08; the D0 prediction's core lib row Math/Complex.pm).  PRE-EXISTING SILENT WRONG on main 06a4b8ba.

REPRODUCERS (probed vs perl 5.40.3; scratch/s535a/pr/p21.pl, p22.pl):

    my $i = 5;
    sub cap { $i }
    sub lp { my @o; for (my $i = 0; $i < 3; $i++) { push @o, "loop $i" } "@o" }
    print lp(), " cap=", cap(), "\n";

perl:          loop 0 loop 1 loop 2 cap=5
base 06a4b8ba: " cap=5"   (the loop never runs: its condition reads the file cell)

    use Math::Complex; my @r = root(16, 4); print "i=", i, " n=", scalar(@r), "\n";

perl:          i=i n=4
base 06a4b8ba: i=4 n=4    (core Math::Complex::root's `for (my $i = 0, my $theta = ...; $i < $n; $i++, ...)` counted in the file's cached `i` constant cell)

WHY: the capture PROMOTER renames a captured file `my $i` to `$i__file__N` and rewrites its later uses, skipping a shadow's scope through the old `_ref_shadowed`, whose sibling walk could not see a C-style `for (my $i ...)` init (a Structure::For in the Compound, never a sibling) -- the same blind spot #4423 was for the requalifier.  The loop's own `my $i` kept its `let`, but its condition and step were renamed to the file cell.

FIX (s535a, 1c port 3): the promoter's skip asks the binder (`Pl::Binder::refers_to_decl`: is this use the binding that declarator makes?), which knows the loop-head scope (perly.y mnexpr).  Guards Pl/t/span-binder-01.t rows 20-21 (both fail on 06a4b8ba).

=== COMPLETED (s536, reviewing session, 2026-11-08) === merged as MAIN-READY-77 fcfce8a5 (s535a, 1c port 3: the span pass on the binder); review probes perl -> main ab0df658 -> tree (scratchpad p535a/a.pl b.pl): tree = perl; no live baseline row keys on this task (CLOSE-WITH-ROWS checked).
